Z||000000||elovio||10-31-2000||11:25 AM||||I have a 1985 Fiero. It runs great! Yet, I have one problem!  The fuel pump remains on even when the vehicle is turned off.  I am currently taking out the fuse to stop the fuel pump from running. I checked the relay and even removed it yet, it still keeps running. I also disconnected the ECM unit and it still keeps running! Any suggestions???||||reg||6
Z||000001||cowans||10-31-2000||12:40 PM||||Elovio,are you sure you are disconnecting the  proper relay. One other thought, the oil pressure sender is wired up to complete the fuel pump circuit, maybe something is amiss with that. You should be able to disconnect the pump by removing the power source to the relay. Not much help, eh! Sandy Maybe give the relay the distance test!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||10-31-2000||03:49 PM||||If the oil pressure switch is bad, the pump may run continously.  There is an extra set of contacts in the oil pressure switch that bypass the ECM and the fuel pump relay to provide power to the pump anytime there is oil pressure present.  Try unplugging the switch and see if the pump quits.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE||||reg||10
